# Apolyx-first UI

Monorepo apps (`apps/*` except the docs app itself) **must not** invent local UI primitives or pull Radix / Base UI / shadcn clones for kit-level controls.

## Rule

1. **Need a component in an app?** Import it from `@altr/apolyx` (workspace). Prefer composition of existing kit parts over new one-offs.
2. **Component missing from Apolyx?** Stop app work. Build it in the kit first with **apollo** (`apollo` / `build apolyx`):
   - Source: `elements/ui-kit` (`@altr/apolyx`)
   - Docs + demo: `apps/apolyx`
   - Registry / CLI when applicable: `elements/apolyx-cli`
   - Hard constraints: no Radix / Base UI; semantic tokens; Storybook + tests + MDX
3. **Document before consume:** update `Docs/feature_list/ui-kit/` (intent if new wave), ship as-built via **docs_man** (`update_docs`) — at least MDX page + registry entry + STATUS / tech_space when non-trivial.
4. **Then** wire the app: `import { … } from "@altr/apolyx"`.

## Do not

- Copy-paste kit components into `apps/<product>/`
- Add `@radix-ui/*`, Base UI, or parallel button/input/select stacks in product apps
- “Temporary” local Dialog / Select / Table “just for this screen”
- Skip docs / registry so only one app knows the API

## Exceptions

- App-specific **screens and layouts** (pages, domain widgets) that only compose Apolyx parts
- One-off marketing illustrations / 3D that are not design-system controls
- `apps/apolyx` itself (the kit docs app)

## Agent routing

| Situation | Agent |
|-----------|--------|
| Missing kit component | **apollo** → then **docs_man** |
| Vault / STATUS / brain after ship | **docs_man** |
| Product app feature using existing kit | normal app work |

